{
  "step_1": "The decision reason considers whether either lottery has a 'sure outcome'—that is, an outcome that occurs with 100% probability. In the given decision problem, Lottery A offers 3000 Euros with 25% probability and 0 Euros with 75% probability. Lottery B offers 4000 Euros with 20% probability and 0 Euros with 80% probability. Neither lottery has a sure outcome (i.e., no outcome occurs with 100% probability). Therefore, the decision reason cannot favor either lottery based on the presence of a sure outcome. The reason would be indifferent between the two lotteries or would not apply at all due to the absence of a sure outcome in either option.",
